// `is` on a union mixing integer widths. The committed VM output is WRONG.
//
// For `x: i32 | i64 | u8`, `tag` must report 1 for a u8, 2 for an i64 and 3
// for a free i32 literal: `1 2 3`, which the native build prints. The VM
// prints `1 1 1`. A VM value records no integer width narrower than its
// 32-bit / 64-bit split, so its `is u8` accepts any integer value, and the
// first test in `tag` matches all three arguments although each call site
// retags its argument with its own width (bytecode snapshot).
//
// Open design question: reject width-mixed integer unions at the typer, let
// `is` treat every integer width alike, or carry the exact width in the VM's
// values.

module "snippet"

import "std/io"

tag :: fn(x: i32 | i64 | u8) -> i32 {
    if x is u8  { return 1 }
    if x is i64 { return 2 }
    return 3
}

main :: fn() -> i32 {
    a: u8: 5
    b: i64: 9999999999
    println("${tag(a)} ${tag(b)} ${tag(7)}")
    return 0
}
